# Conductivity follows ion concentration after mixing
# Equal final water volumes receive increasing sodium-chloride amounts. This
# isolates ion concentration from volume before the conductivity readings.
register lv2
add v1 water 200mL
new
add v2 water 200mL
new
mix v1 1 v2 1 into v3
measure v3 conductivity
new
add v4 water 200mL
add v4 NaCl 0.001mol
new
add v5 water 200mL
new
mix v4 1 v5 1 into v6
measure v6 conductivity
new
add v7 water 200mL
add v7 NaCl 0.002mol
new
add v8 water 200mL
new
mix v7 1 v8 1 into v9
measure v9 conductivity
new
add v10 water 200mL
add v10 NaCl 0.004mol
new
add v11 water 200mL
new
mix v10 1 v11 1 into v12
measure v12 conductivity
# Conductivity is estimated from the computed ions; cell constant, electrode
# polarisation, calibration drift and temperature compensation are absent.
